TOKEN tinybird_read READ

DESCRIPTION >
What D1 was doing around a moment: per second, per service, route and query,
the calls started, their summed and longest wall time, D1's own SQL time,
rows read and failures. Pass `at` (UTC, e.g. 2026-11-23 13:02:06) and
optionally `before_seconds` (default 60) and `after_seconds` (default 10).
The culprit shows up before the stall; the stall shows as long durations and
failures on the victims.

NODE d1_stall_context_seconds
SQL >
    %
    SELECT
        timestamp AS second,
        service,
        route_path,
        method,
        query_id,
        any(substring(q.sql, 1, 300)) AS sql,
        sum(e.calls) AS calls,
        sum(e.total_ms) AS total_ms,
        max(e.max_ms) AS max_ms,
        round(sum(e.sql_ms), 1) AS sql_ms,
        sum(e.rows_read) AS rows_read,
        sum(e.rows_written) AS rows_written,
        sumIf(e.calls, error_code != '') AS failed,
        groupUniqArrayIf(error_code, error_code != '') AS error_codes
    FROM d1_call_event AS e
    LEFT JOIN (SELECT query_id, any(sql) AS sql FROM d1_query GROUP BY query_id) AS q
        USING (query_id)
    WHERE environment = {{ String(environment, 'production') }}
        AND timestamp >= toDateTime({{ String(at, '2026-11-23 13:02:06', required=True) }}, 'UTC')
            - toIntervalSecond({{ UInt32(before_seconds, 60) }})
        AND timestamp < toDateTime({{ String(at, '2026-11-23 13:02:06', required=True) }}, 'UTC')
            + toIntervalSecond({{ UInt32(after_seconds, 10) }})
    GROUP BY second, service, route_path, method, query_id
    ORDER BY second, total_ms DESC

TYPE endpoint
